messages.text:
Got it: no more proving. I now measure and optimize every image on the page, and bring it to you as a proposal. ETA: about 3 hours.

- Step 1, list (now): every picture, background, overlay and texture on the whole page: file type, size in bytes, real size vs what a phone shows, how many a phone can ever see, and the blend/grain/blur layers on top.
- Step 2, Chrome counts: how often each picture is drawn and unpacked during one scroll (counts only, no timing).
- Step 3, optimize in my test copy (the real files stay untouched):
  - shrink each picture to what a phone shows (3x screens);
  - lighter formats Safari supports (AVIF/WebP), with the source cited;
  - bake the grain/blend overlays into the picture where it looks the same;
  - skip pictures a phone never shows (the 11 hidden wall photos);
  - loading hints.
- Step 4, proposal with Try-it pages (normal vs optimized on your phone): bytes saved, a pixel check of the look, and Chrome slow-frame counts.
- New file formats change pixels slightly, so you decide; phone timing only after you pick.

What you need to do: finish the swipe pair on the phone when ready (it waits for you). Nothing else now.
